	(footprint "pluto_rx2_8way_v4:SMA_Vertical_5.08sq_D1.4"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "f653719e-737a-4193-884b-5f790969a982")
		(at 40.75 33.1)
		(descr "Kinghelm KH-SMA-KE-Z vertical THT SMA flange JACK (female, 1/4-36UNEF). AUTHORED from drawing sheet 2/2 dated 2021.08.10: PCB layout inset gives 5-D1.4 - four corner holes on a 5.08 x 5.08 mm square plus ONE at the centre; rear view gives 4-SQ0.9 posts on the same 5.08 square inside a 6.5 x 6.5 mm flange with a 4.2 mm insulator face. D1.4 not D1.3: a 0.9 mm SQUARE post has a 1.273 mm diagonal, so D1.3 leaves 0.014 mm radial clearance and D1.4 leaves 0.064 mm. Pad 1 = centre = RF signal; pads 2-5 = the four ground posts. The centre pad carries a 0.80 mm LOCAL CLEARANCE, which is what opens the REQUIRED >=3.5 mm antipad in every ground plane (1.9 + 2 x 0.8 = 3.5) - a minimum-DRC 2.6 mm antipad costs ~5.6 dB of return loss at 6 GHz. Ground posts are set zone_connect SOLID: the four posts ARE the launch return path and a thermal spoke is not one.")
		(tags "SMA jack vertical THT connector RF 50ohm 5.08 flange Kinghelm")
